-- cmd: check
-- exit: 1
-- A field read nothing decides is the one error of its function: what its
-- result leaves undecided (`p.a + p.d` owes trait 'Number') is not
-- refused again, in the function or at its call.
type A { a: Int, d: Int }
fn i(p) { p.a + p.d }
fn main() { println(i(A { a: 1, d: 2 })) }
